---
description: Supabase, persistence, schema, and user-data isolation rules.
globs: '{src/infrastructure/**,supabase/**,src/features/**/api/**}'
alwaysApply: false
---

Read `docs/database-model.md` before data-layer work.

- MVP authentication uses an anonymous Supabase user with no visible login screen.
- Every user-owned row must be protected by Row Level Security.
- Database schema changes must be represented by versioned SQL migrations.
- Use English snake_case table and column names.
- Do not expose service-role keys in the frontend.
- Do not place raw Supabase calls in React presentation components.
- Validate external data at the infrastructure boundary.
- Keep seed data separate from production data.
- Use neutral technical keys and Polish display labels for disciplines, block types, tasks, and combinations.
- Historical workout snapshots must remain stable after library records change.
